<VI _name="lvai_bind_pane_typedef_instr_v2.vi" description="INSTRUMENTED + ORDERING-FIXED copy of lvai_bind_pane_typedef\2C Round7. The original helper leaves the SAVE CHAIN and the BIND LOOP with no dataflow edge between them\3A both become ready at the Controls[] read\2C so Save.Instrument can complete before the Replace ever runs\2C which was measured as terminalsBound=2 with every error cluster 0 and ZERO typedefs in the saved file\2C the binding reaching the file only on a SECOND run. THE FIX IS ONE EDGE\3A Index Array over the bind loop's replace-errors output\2C chained into LVClass.Open's error in\2C so no save can start before the loop finished. Everything else is the v1 instrumented helper\3A five read-back stages (before, after Replace in memory, after Save.Instrument on a fresh reopen, after the class Save on another fresh reopen) plus a Replace liveness probe whose error 1055 proves the Replace really replaced.">
